or Safe Democratic", "Prediction markets price Shapiro's win odds at 96-98%"], "rationale": "Polls from Siena, Quinnipiac, Franklin & Marshall and even Republican-sponsored firms all show Shapiro ahead by double digits, he has vastly outraised and outspent Garrity, and every major rater rates the race Solid or Safe Democratic. Pennsylvania's slight Republican lean is swamped by Shapiro's incumbency standing.", "watch": "Only an extraordinary late development, such as a major scandal or a sharp national backlash, would meaningfully narrow a lead this large.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Josh Shapiro seeks a second term as Pennsylvania governor against State Treasurer Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Pennsylvania leans slightly Republican at the presidential level, but Shapiro enters with the advantages of incumbency, high name recognition, and a large fundraising edge; reporting through late September describes him as vastly outraising and outspending Garrity.\n\nPolling has been unusually one-sided. Surveys from Siena, Quinnipiac, Franklin & Marshall, and PennLive since mid-summer all show Shapiro ahead by double digits, most by 16 to 27 points, and aggregated estimates put his lead around 22 to 25 points. Every major race rater classifies the contest as Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets give Shapiro roughly a 96 to 98 percent chance of winning. Garrity, a credible statewide officeholder, has struggled to close the name-recognition and money gaps.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date":